With `jinja: true` the preamble goes through the full context env: a `{{ … }}` expression resolves
against the merged config, and `{% include %}` pulls a partial from the playbook's own directory —
the first link of the body's loader chain. The step section is unaffected: opting into Jinja does
not embed any body.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  fx_label: hermetic label
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-jinja-preamble/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-jinja-preamble
title: Jinja Preamble
summary: Preamble rendered through the context.
jinja: true
---

Preamble label {{ config.core.fx_label }}.

{% include "shared.md" %}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-jinja-preamble/shared.md --
Included partial content.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-jinja-preamble/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  one: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-jinja-preamble/one/prompt.md --
---
name: one
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-jinja-preamble
